{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>מודע</b> ('kinsman-acquaintance'). A known kinsman, like 'and לבינה תקרא מודע' (Isaiah 40:14)." "<b>לאישה</b> ('to her'). From אישה ('her husband'), and the lamed is like 'אחי הוא לי אמרי' (Jeremiah 22:5)." "<b>בועז</b>. Our Rabbis of blessed memory said that he is Ibzan, who judged Israel."], :book :ruth, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {1 "Ibn Ezra cites the lamed of לאישה as lamed of relationship/appurtenance, illustrating with Jeremiah 22:5; rendered in citation order."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Ruth -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/ruth"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:43:38.932197863Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}